      "id": "S3",
      "status": "pass",
      "analysis": "The nine original mathematical modules were read in full. They prove actual binomial smoothing, peak decay and total variation, actual rectangle telescopes and R factorization, then extend vanishing from the two algebraic ranges to their norm closure using uniform bounds. The comparison theorem proves both directions for every x and z. The constructed recovery on the genuine Z+Y has uniqueness, range Z, kernel Y and norm at most KT*KS; the actual quotient inverse is defined only on q(Z). Quotient infimum approximation gives both stability inequalities, and completeness plus antilipschitzness proves q(Z) and its inverse image D closed. No Hilbert, reflexivity, finite-dimensional or unclosed-range substitution enters.",
